      ":question/id": "5a03e52f-a789-58b8-8cc0-a47e970671ff",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 64}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First factor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\nx^{2} + 64=64(1+(\\frac{1}{64})x^{2})\n$$\n\nUse the linear substitution $u=\\frac{x}{8}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{8},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(8)\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x^{2} + 64}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\frac{1}{64}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(\\frac{x}{8})^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{64}(8)\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{8}\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}}{8}+C \\\\  &= \\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(\\frac{x}{8} \\right)}}{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
